=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: a push-only benchmark job beside a reworded pytest step disables nothing that ran
origin: issue #181 bound, from the review of PR #191 — the disabled predicate needs the runner that
origin2: stopped to be the runner that was parked. `pytest` -> `pytest --cov=src` still runs the suite,
origin3: and the new benchmark job never ran on a pull request at base.
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest --cov=src
  benchmark:
    if: github.event_name == 'push'
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest benchmarks --benchmark-only
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn"}]
